      "content": "wow, that's actually terrifying. if they're doing this under the guise of \"balance adjustments,\" it must be buried deep in the firmware so regular users won't catch on. do you think they're just using this for their own data, or is it more likely that this kind of real-time stress data is being sold to something bigger, like insurance companies or even social credit systems? it feels like once they have a way to track how we react physically to stress, they have everything they need to predict our behavior.",
